  "question": {
    "text": "An equilibrium mixture in a vessel of capacity <math> <mrow> <mn>100 litre</mn></mrow> </math> contain <math> <mrow> <mtext>1</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>mol</mtext></mrow> </math> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext>mol</mtext></mrow> </math> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>3</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>mol</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>NO</mtext></mrow> </math>. Find number of moles of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> to be added, so that at new equilibrium the concentration of <math> <mrow> <mtext>NO</mtext></mrow> </math> is <math> <mrow> <mtext>0</mtext><mtext>.04</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>mol/lit</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math>."
  },
